<title>TUNISIA: Tunisia's citrus exports down.</title>
<headline>Tunisia's citrus exports down.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tunisia's exports of citrus fruits this season were 16,084 tonnes worth 13 million dinars, down from 21,732 tonnes worth 15.2 million dinars the previous season, Agriculture Minister Mabrouk Bahri said on Friday.</p>
<p>Output was put at 211,000 tonnes this season, down by five percent from 221,000 tonnes last year.</p>
<p>France is Tunisia's traditional market for citrus. ($=1.1024 dinar)</p>
<p>Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
